{"id":"f27160aa-b4e2-450f-b006-594389c86887","object":"chat.completion","created":1784808451,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    payload = case\\n    if 'word_token_indices' not in payload or 'word_labels' not in payload or 'token_count' not in payload:\\n        raise ValueError('Missing required fields')\\n    word_token_indices = payload['word_token_indices']\\n    word_labels = payload['word_labels']\\n    token_count = payload['token_count']\\n    if len(word_token_indices) != len(word_labels):\\n        raise ValueError('Mismatch between word groups and labels')\\n    for label in word_labels:\\n        if label not in (0, 1):\\n            raise ValueError('Invalid label value')\\n    token_mask = [None] * token_count\\n    for idx_group, indices in enumerate(word_token_indices):\\n        label = word_labels[idx_group]\\n        for j in indices:\\n            if not (0 <= j < token_count):\\n                raise ValueError(f'Token index {j} out of range')\\n            if token_mask[j] is not None:\\n                raise ValueError(f'Overlapping token index {j}')\\n            token_mask[j] = label\\n    for i, val in enumerate(token_mask):\\n        if val is None:\\n            raise ValueError(f'Uncovered token index {i}')\\n    token_label_vector = token_mask\\n    retained_indices = [i for i, v in enumerate(token_label_vector) if v == 1]\\n    return {'token_label_vector': token_label_vector, 'retained_indices': retained_indices}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing Python source code for solve(case). The task: word_label_alignment. Input case has word_token_indices (list of lists of ints), word_labels (list of ints 0/1), token_count (int). Must validate: exactly one label per word group; broadcast to token indices; reject overlapping/out-of-range/uncovered indices; keep tokens with label=1; return full token-label vector and retained indices. Must not mutate case. Use only standard library. Return JSON-serializable object. Raise ValueError for invalid.\n\nWe'll implement solve(case) that:\n\n1. Validate fields exist: word_token_indices, word_labels, token_count. Also check word_labels length == len(word_token_indices).\n2. Compute token_mask of length token_count, initialized to None or -1.\n3. For each word group i, for each token index j in word_token_indices[i]:\n   - Check j in [0, token_count-1], else raise ValueError.\n   - Check token_mask[j] is None (not already assigned), else raise ValueError (overlapping).\n   - Assign token_mask[j] = word_labels[i].\n4. After processing all, check no token_mask entry is None (uncovered). That is, all indices 0..token_count-1 must be assigned exactly once.\n5. Then full_token_label_vector = token_mask (list of ints 0/1).\n6. retained_indices = [i for i, v in enumerate(full_token_label_vector) if v == 1].\n7. Return a dict with keys: \"token_mask\" (list of ints 0/1), \"retained_indices\" (list of ints). Or maybe \"full_token_label_vector\"? The description says \"full token-label vector and retained indices\". I'll name them \"token_label_vector\" and \"retained_indices\". But we need to match expected output? Probably just return dict with those keys. The problem statement: \"Return the full token-label vector and retained indices.\" So we can return a dict with those two fields. Also maybe include other fields for audit? But it says \"Preserve every source identifier needed to audit the decision, and compute aggregate values from the returned primitive decisions rather than from a second approximation.\" However, we are only required to return JSON-serializable object; we can include case_id etc. But the instruction: \"Return one JSON object with exactly one key, `implementation`.\" That's the wrapper. The solve function itself must return a JSON-serializable object. We'll keep simple: { \"token_label_vector\": [...], \"retained_indices\": [...] }. Add any extra? Not necessary. But \"Preserve every source identifier\" might mean we should include case's _case_nonce or something? The function returns the result, not the audit trail. I'll stick to minimal.\n\nEdge cases: word_token_indices may not be sorted? But we just process in order. Ensure stable order: we process groups in given order, tokens in given order. That satisfies \"stable_order\".\n\nAlso need to validate that word_labels are 0 or 1? Probably yes, but can check.\n\nReturn only JSON-serializable: lists, ints.\n\nRaise ValueError for infeasible.\n\nWrite Python code.\n\nNow produce JSON with escaped string."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":941,"completion_tokens":1045,"total_tokens":1986,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":896},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":698},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":896,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":45},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}